keywords:
  - systemic sclerosis
  - scleroderma
  - single nuclei multiome
  - snATAC-seq
  - dissociation bias
  - cell type composition
  - GSE312129
abstract: >-
  Reprocessing of GSE312129 finds that fibroblast nuclei are recovered from
  systemic sclerosis skin at roughly one sixth the rate of healthy skin
  (median 6.1 versus 38.3 percent of quality controlled nuclei, exact
  Mann-Whitney p = 0.014), in the direction opposite to the disease. The
  asymmetry is corroborated by COL1A1 detection and is a composition confound
  for between group comparisons drawn from this dataset. Also included is the
  complete record of the preregistered RUNX paralog analysis that did not
  reach its donor floor and was stopped.
